      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In the kitchen, the cooks are enjoying a rare moment of peace and quiet. Senya notes how great the atmosphere is today, and Fedya quickly points out the reason. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не думал, что тут так классно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Везде классно, когда нет Макса.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, сегодня очень тихо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Нам надо работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я просто отдыхаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф может прийти.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф сейчас занят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Всё равно, давай работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, я иду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Где мой нож?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он на столе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Спасибо, я вижу.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я не думал, что тут так классно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I didn't think it was so great here.' The key word here means 'I', which Senya combines with 'thought'. Fedya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Везде классно, когда нет Макса.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is great everywhere when there is no Max.' Fedya puts 'everywhere' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'great'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, сегодня очень тихо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, it is very quiet today.' Here 'today' sets up the idea, while 'easy' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Нам надо работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We need to work.' You'll hear 'us' all the time in the show, here connected with 'to work'. Then Senya replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я просто отдыхаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am just resting.' A compact expression built around 'I' and 'am resting'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Шеф может прийти.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The chef can come.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'chef, boss' paired with the verb for 'can'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф сейчас занят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The chef is busy now.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'chef, boss' paired with the adverb for 'now'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Всё равно, давай работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Anyway, let's work.' Fedya puts 'the same' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'let's'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, я иду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good, I am coming.' The key word here means 'good', which Senya combines with 'I'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Где мой нож?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where is my knife?' In Russian, 'where' leads into 'knife' in a very natural everyday phrasing. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Он на столе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is on the table.' Listen for the word meaning 'he' right alongside 'table' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Спасибо, я вижу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you, I see it.' Notice the word order: 'thank you' comes first, and 'see' finishes the sentence. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
